WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.500
- What's going on?

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.670
- [Mark] Okay, Suicidal?

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:08.503
- Yeah.

00:00:08.503 --> 00:00:09.853
- [Mark] So where'd you grow up?

00:00:09.853 --> 00:00:11.130
- What you say?

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:11.999
- [Mark] Where'd you grow up?

00:00:11.999 --> 00:00:13.337
- Where'd I grow up at?

00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:15.089
- [Mark] What part of town?

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:17.147
I was born in the wild, though,

00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:19.040
but I was raised in five deuce.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:19.873
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:22.410
- I said I was born in the
wild, but I was raised in L.A.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.243
- [Mark] Oh, okay.

00:00:23.243 --> 00:00:28.160
And what age were you
when you entered the gang?

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.630
- My hood?

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.559
I was always in the hood.

00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:33.024
- [Mark] But what age were you when-

00:00:33.024 --> 00:00:34.630
- At the age of fourteen.
Five Deuce Hoover, ya hear?

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:36.247
- [Mark] And how old were you

00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:37.080
when you first got involved in the gang?

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.290
- I was 14.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.123
- [Mark] 14?

00:00:39.123 --> 00:00:39.956
- Yeah.

00:00:41.116 --> 00:00:42.041
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.850
You had both parents, one parent?

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.180
- Nah, my mom was sick.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.123
Ah, shit, here we go.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:50.880
Nah, my pops was doing a life sentence.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.021
He died in prison, man.

00:00:53.021 --> 00:00:53.854
- [Mark] You were a kid?

00:00:53.854 --> 00:00:55.160
- He left me at age two, homie.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:55.993
- [Mark] Your dad died in prison?

00:00:55.993 --> 00:00:57.860
- Yeah, age two. He left me at age two.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.857
He died. I was 19, so.

00:01:00.842 --> 00:01:02.973
I only saw him twice a year.

00:01:02.973 --> 00:01:04.877
- [Mark] Mm hmm.

00:01:04.877 --> 00:01:07.100
And your mom? What's the story as well?

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.541
Naw, she was good. She's good now.

00:01:08.541 --> 00:01:10.631
She was a crackhead. You
know what I'm sayin'?

00:01:10.631 --> 00:01:12.057
She's good now though.
- Oh, okay.

00:01:12.057 --> 00:01:13.170
She go to church. She's a changed woman.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.946
- [Mark] So the gang was
like a natural place for you.

00:01:14.946 --> 00:01:16.393
It's my family. It's my family.

00:01:16.393 --> 00:01:17.226
Man, it's hot.

00:01:17.226 --> 00:01:19.330
- [Mark] It was your family.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.210
- It always will be until I die.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.690
- [Mark] And prison time,
have you done any prison time?

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:27.947
- Yeah, 15 years straight, holmes.

00:01:27.947 --> 00:01:28.780
- [Mark] Oh, yeah?

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.740
- Yeah.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.317
- [Mark] What was that for?

00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:34.734
- Home invasion, robbery, shit like that.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:36.873
- [Mark] What age was that?

00:01:36.873 --> 00:01:37.820
- When I was 18.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.281
- [Mark] 18?

00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:40.114
- Yeah.

00:01:40.114 --> 00:01:41.690
- [Mark] Did you finish
high school at all?

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:45.825
Nah, I left after 11th grade.

00:01:45.825 --> 00:01:47.520
At 11th grade, I left.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.827
- [Mark] Oh, at 11th grade?

00:01:48.827 --> 00:01:51.500
- I caught a charge, so I couldn't finish.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.412
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.245
- [Mark] Right.

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.310
- I got my GED, though.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.143
- [Mark] Oh, good.

00:01:55.143 --> 00:01:56.016
- Yeah, I got my GED.

00:01:56.016 --> 00:01:59.550
I got prison, but I got my GED. (chuckles)

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.309
Yeah, I had to get that.

00:02:01.309 --> 00:02:02.142
I can say one thing,

00:02:02.142 --> 00:02:02.975
you know what I'm sayin'?

00:02:02.975 --> 00:02:03.808
- [Mark] Yes.

00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:06.014
- I'm glad, you know?

00:02:06.014 --> 00:02:07.907
- [Mark] That's pretty hard
on pretty much everyone

00:02:07.907 --> 00:02:09.042
in these situations.

00:02:09.042 --> 00:02:09.875
- Yeah.

00:02:11.922 --> 00:02:13.167
It's hot.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.770
- [Mark] But you still have
contact with your family?

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:18.608
- My mom, yeah. Hell, yeah, I love my mom.

00:02:18.608 --> 00:02:19.743
I love my mom, ya know what I mean?

00:02:19.743 --> 00:02:20.703
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:20.703 --> 00:02:23.123
- I love my mom, always, you know?

00:02:23.123 --> 00:02:26.860
No matter what she did,
she was always by me.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.910
You know what I mean?

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:32.040
She was always by me.
Ya know what I'm sayin'?

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.040
But it was hard, you know?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.370
Especially growing up. Nobody was there.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.203
Ya feel me?

00:02:36.203 --> 00:02:37.036
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:37.036 --> 00:02:37.869
- Very hard, ya know.

00:02:37.869 --> 00:02:41.900
It's still hard, but I live
and die in L.A. (chuckles)

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.270
- [Mark] Yeah, you've seen
some crazy stuff being

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.688
in the gang, right?

00:02:45.688 --> 00:02:49.331
Lost friends, stuff like that?

00:02:49.331 --> 00:02:50.475
- To see crazy stuff, you
don't have to be in a gang.

00:02:50.475 --> 00:02:54.100
You see crazy stuff everywhere
you go. The world's crazy.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.147
Ya know what I'm sayin'?

00:02:55.147 --> 00:02:57.247
You don't got to be in a gang to be crazy.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:58.963
Ya know what I'm saying?

00:02:58.963 --> 00:02:59.796
Well, it's just that in a gang,

00:02:59.796 --> 00:03:01.570
you recognize craziness.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.403
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:02.403 --> 00:03:04.200
- That's all. You recognize it.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.589
- [Mark] What personality traits
do you think a person needs

00:03:08.589 --> 00:03:09.422
to survive in a gang?
- Just be real, man.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.920
Just be real. Be you, be you.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.760
That's all. Be you.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.331
Ya know what I'm saying? Don't be fake.

00:03:15.331 --> 00:03:17.290
Don't try to pretend to be somebody else.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.060
You get more respect.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.763
You live longer just being you.

00:03:22.682 --> 00:03:23.599
That's all.

00:03:24.618 --> 00:03:25.467
That's what it's all about, ya know?

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.530
Not to get caught up.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.890
Everybody wanna be like their super...

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.250
The movie shit. Ya know what I'm saying?

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.465
Nah, it aint about that. It's
about survival, that's all.

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:37.070
That's all it's about, survival.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:38.659
Take your own. That's all it's about.

00:03:38.659 --> 00:03:40.133
Ya know what I mean?

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:40.966
Just be able to survive.

00:03:40.966 --> 00:03:43.153
If you don't survive, you get run over.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.330
Just not by gangs;

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.160
by anybody, police,
anybody could get run over.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.630
Ya know? That's what it's about?

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.880
- [Mark] So when you were in
your twenties, teens, whatever-

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.553
- My twenties. I didn't see no twenties.

00:03:58.553 --> 00:04:00.330
My whole twenties, I was in prison.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.992
I didn't see not one day in my twenties.

00:04:01.992 --> 00:04:02.950
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.297
- Yeah, I never saw one day.

00:04:05.297 --> 00:04:06.955
Never seen one day in
my twenties, ya hear?

00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:09.007
All I saw was bars and gates.

00:04:09.007 --> 00:04:10.539
- [Mark] All of your twenties,
you were still in prison?

00:04:10.539 --> 00:04:12.450
- All the twenties, all
I saw was bars and gates.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:13.283
Ching, ching.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.970
- [Mark] Well, obviously, gang life

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:16.900
in prison still exists.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:17.961
It's just different here.

00:04:17.961 --> 00:04:20.243
- This is a world inside a world.

00:04:21.368 --> 00:04:23.675
That's all it is. Ya feel me?

00:04:23.675 --> 00:04:27.960
Anything that goes
outside, you do it inside.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.290
Well, the guards is gangsters...

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.420
Nine out of ten, the
guards is more gangsters

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.588
than the inmates. (chuckles)

00:04:33.588 --> 00:04:34.421
Ya feel me?

00:04:34.421 --> 00:04:35.254
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:35.254 --> 00:04:36.462
- That's how it is.

00:04:36.462 --> 00:04:37.295
For real. (chuckles)

00:04:37.295 --> 00:04:39.485
- [Mark] Tell us some stories

00:04:39.485 --> 00:04:41.593
about some of the violence you
saw when you were in prison.

00:04:41.593 --> 00:04:43.300
You saw some crazy stuff, I'm sure.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.284
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:46.284 --> 00:04:47.618
There's a lot of crazy shit.

00:04:47.618 --> 00:04:49.770
There's a lot of crazy
shit, though, ya know?

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.743
It is what it is. (chuckles)

00:04:51.743 --> 00:04:53.160
It is what it is.

00:04:55.158 --> 00:04:59.520
- [Mark] Do you feel safer
being out of prison than in?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.327
- Shit! (chuckles)

00:05:02.327 --> 00:05:04.663
That's a good question. ( chuckles)

00:05:04.663 --> 00:05:06.237
A damn good question. (chuckles)

00:05:06.237 --> 00:05:07.655
That's a good question, man.

00:05:07.655 --> 00:05:12.655
Do I feel safer out here
than in prison? (laughs)

00:05:15.027 --> 00:05:16.979
I'll tell you one thing, in prison,

00:05:16.979 --> 00:05:18.618
it's that question there,

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:19.708
it's why I'm laughing at that

00:05:19.708 --> 00:05:23.006
cause in prison, you know what to expect.

00:05:23.006 --> 00:05:26.334
You wake up, you gotta tie your shoes,

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:27.167
you know what you gotta do,

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:28.453
but out here, you don't
know what to expect.

00:05:30.209 --> 00:05:32.690
The closer ones be the dangerous ones.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.520
Ya know what I mean?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.530
The protectors of the
city are more dangerous

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:42.280
than the criminals, I guess.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.400
So how do I put this?

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.040
You go to the grocery
store, you get locked up.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.561
Or so just cops who don't like me,

00:05:48.561 --> 00:05:50.112
they throw shit on me.

00:05:50.112 --> 00:05:53.723
So safe? (chuckles)

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.143
- [Mark] When were you last in prison?

00:05:59.508 --> 00:06:00.341
- What's that?

00:06:00.341 --> 00:06:02.077
- [Mark] How long has it been
since you were in prison?

00:06:02.077 --> 00:06:04.470
- You mean my term or
just going to prison?

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:05.468
- [Mark] When was the
last time you were...

00:06:05.468 --> 00:06:07.130
When did you get out?

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:11.817
- My term, at age 33, but
I did time after that.

00:06:11.817 --> 00:06:13.116
Ya know what I'm sayin'?

00:06:13.116 --> 00:06:14.623
But a long term, like a
year here, and two there.

00:06:14.623 --> 00:06:16.226
Ya know what I'm sayin'?

00:06:16.226 --> 00:06:18.275
Between 14 years old, man,

00:06:18.275 --> 00:06:20.142
the God honest truth,

00:06:20.142 --> 00:06:22.642
I've probably saw like
three years on the streets.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:24.343
- [Mark] Only 3 years?
- Yeah.

00:06:24.343 --> 00:06:25.374
- [Mark] Since you were 14?

00:06:25.374 --> 00:06:26.550
- I'm about to be 39.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.383
- [Mark] Jesus.

00:06:27.383 --> 00:06:28.450
- Maybe three years.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.283
- [Mark] And how old are you now?

00:06:29.283 --> 00:06:30.417
- I'll be 39.

00:06:30.417 --> 00:06:31.250
- [Mark] 39?

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.146
- I only say three
years, about three years.

00:06:33.146 --> 00:06:38.110
Yes, I only saw three
years. Word. (laughs)

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:38.943
- [Mark] So do you have kids of your own?

00:06:38.943 --> 00:06:41.756
- No, I haven't had a chance for that yet.

00:06:41.756 --> 00:06:43.356
- [Mark] You never had a
chance. You were in prison.

00:06:43.356 --> 00:06:47.256
- I'm glad though. I'd be a
fucked up daddy. (chuckles)

00:06:47.256 --> 00:06:49.470
- [Mark] Yeah. What do you
see for yourself in the next-

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.560
- Right now, though?

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:51.393
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:51.393 --> 00:06:52.340
- I ask myself...

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.173
recognizing the truth,

00:06:53.173 --> 00:06:54.761
that that's why I slowed down, man.

00:06:54.761 --> 00:06:58.651
Ya feeling me? Like I'm more mature now.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.930
I might still have the
same attitude a little bit,

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.840
but as in gentleness, I'm there.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:07.840
As in understanding of society
giving a chance to help you,

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:10.911
I'm starting to see that.
I go to church sometimes.

00:07:10.911 --> 00:07:11.744
Ya know what I'm saying?

00:07:11.744 --> 00:07:14.663
I can't do it by myself. I can't. I can't.

00:07:14.663 --> 00:07:16.080
I tried, I can't.

00:07:19.858 --> 00:07:22.400
I ain't gonna lie,
sometimes you'll catch me

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.371
or someone reaching out to me, ya know?

00:07:25.371 --> 00:07:29.550
Getting a little help
sometimes, and I listen.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.780
But it's hard to really listen

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:34.136
and try to follow what
you listening cause...

00:07:34.136 --> 00:07:35.320
At least, I got to church Sunday.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:39.055
I'm coming out. It's wartime.

00:07:39.055 --> 00:07:40.270
You feel me? (chuckles)

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.103
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:07:41.103 --> 00:07:42.217
You can't go out on the streets and say,

00:07:42.217 --> 00:07:44.618
"God save when shit's going down."

00:07:44.618 --> 00:07:45.602
- [Mark] Right.

00:07:45.602 --> 00:07:47.900
- It is what it is. It is what it is.

00:07:52.727 --> 00:07:53.972
- [Mark] And where are you staying now?

00:07:53.972 --> 00:07:54.805
Where do you live now?

00:07:54.805 --> 00:07:56.086
- On the streets, skid row.

00:07:56.086 --> 00:07:56.919
- [Mark] Oh, (indistinct)

00:07:56.919 --> 00:07:57.836
- Skid row.

00:08:02.413 --> 00:08:04.247
- [Mark] Are you still active in the gang?

00:08:04.247 --> 00:08:06.262
- Until I die. Until I die.

00:08:06.262 --> 00:08:07.095
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:08:07.095 --> 00:08:09.876
- Why not? At least, somebody love me.

00:08:09.876 --> 00:08:11.043
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:13.453
So if you get called on to do out

00:08:13.453 --> 00:08:15.015
to do whatever you need
to do for the gang,

00:08:15.015 --> 00:08:16.043
you're there.

00:08:17.279 --> 00:08:20.963
- I can't say that. I
ain't gonna gang bang.

00:08:20.963 --> 00:08:23.990
I ain't dumb. I'm getting to old for that.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:28.436
When I say as in, but as in loving,

00:08:28.436 --> 00:08:30.390
giving them advices.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:37.670
You feel me? I don't know. (mumbling)

00:08:40.133 --> 00:08:42.458
I'm not in for that. I'd be a damn fool.

00:08:42.458 --> 00:08:43.820
I'm too old for that. I
don't got time for that.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:45.800
I did mean, but yeah, I'm still active,

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:48.120
as in they're still my family.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:49.666
They're still my nephews,
you know what I mean?

00:08:49.666 --> 00:08:50.499
- [Mark] Right.

00:08:50.499 --> 00:08:54.786
- Somebody gotta lead them
or teach them the right way.

00:08:54.786 --> 00:08:56.705
If I don't do it, then who will?

00:08:56.705 --> 00:08:59.467
So I mean, active, you would say, yeah,

00:08:59.467 --> 00:09:01.310
but as in doing gang shit?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.143
No. Hell, no.

00:09:03.676 --> 00:09:06.210
I'm not a coward, man.
Bloods is my friends too.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:07.220
Ya know what I'm saying?

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.326
Friends to me, do ya know what I meant?

00:09:09.326 --> 00:09:12.630
I look at it as in, "Why kill each other?"

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:13.463
Ya know what I mean?

00:09:13.463 --> 00:09:14.830
- [Mark] Do you have regrets about-

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:18.855
- Hell, yeah! You don't even
have to finish that. (laughs)

00:09:18.855 --> 00:09:19.688
- [Mark] It goes without saying?

00:09:19.688 --> 00:09:23.034
- Yeah, a lot of regrets,
man. A lot of regrets.

00:09:23.034 --> 00:09:26.275
I'd take shit back. I wish I could.

00:09:26.275 --> 00:09:27.525
I wish I could.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.900
I made a lot of dumb choices.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.193
I understand that what they doing now is

00:09:35.193 --> 00:09:36.026
what I used to do,

00:09:36.026 --> 00:09:40.740
so I'd be a hypocrite
saying they're doing wrong.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.220
I was doing the same shit,
you know what I'm sayin'?

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:44.463
Hard-headed, no father,

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.006
so it's like, I couldn't
tell no gangsters,

00:09:47.006 --> 00:09:49.610
"You, what you're doing is wrong."

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.623
Nah, they gotta learn it their way.

